 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? Yes, it does. It' called expose learning. The more times you see something, the more likely it is to stick. You can still learn from a pure watch phase. Just focus on the story, and try guessing the words you don't know from context. Ideally several whole series, at least four or five. An intense week of three or four series is much better than letting them simmer months. Great. Lots of short stories or a TV series is better than a long film. DVDs and streaming often have the subtitle file separate from the video, which you can open separately much faster.",
